From: RDNA3-Hackintosh
Subject: [PATCH] ac: RADV_ATTR_RING_BIG_PAGE=0 turns the attribute ring's BIG_PAGE off

Card run 2026-10-26g (DRIVER-PLAN N57): Terminal's glyphs break at draw
time on the GPU, a contiguous run of exactly 18 instances of one draw gets
garbage varyings while the draw's inputs are right on the GPU and the same
SPIR-V is pixel-perfect under Linux RADV on this card. On GFX11 the
vertex attributes reach the pixel shader through the attribute ring, a
DISCARDABLE VRAM BO that ac_emit_cp_gfx11_ge_rings declares with
SPI_ATTRIBUTE_RING_SIZE.BIG_PAGE = discardable_allows_big_page: the SPI
then translates the ring in 64 KiB pages, which holds only when the
kernel placed the ring in contiguous VRAM and mapped it with matching
PTE fragments. The macOS kernel driver's GPUVM writes 4 KiB PTEs without
fragments by default (amdgpu always uses them).

RADV_ATTR_RING_BIG_PAGE=0 clears discardable_allows_big_page (its only
user is that register) and says so on stderr; the Metal plugin sets it
from NVMTL_ATTR_RING_BIG_PAGE=0 (the ladder's `attrring` rung). Unset or
any other value: upstream behaviour.
---
diff --git a/src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c b/src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c
index 895e38b..4bda3e5 100644
--- a/src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c
+++ b/src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c
@@ -1641,6 +1641,18 @@ ac_query_gpu_info(int fd, void *dev_p, struct radeon_info *info,
    info->discardable_allows_big_page = info->gfx_level >= GFX10_3 && info->gfx_level < GFX12 &&
                                        info->has_dedicated_vram;
 
+   /* RADV_ATTR_RING_BIG_PAGE=0: SPI_ATTRIBUTE_RING_SIZE.BIG_PAGE off, the GFX11 attribute ring is translated in 4 KiB
+    * pages (an A/B for the macOS kernel driver's placement and PTEs of the ring BO). Unset or any other value: as upstream.
+    */
+   {
+      const char *big_page = debug_get_option("RADV_ATTR_RING_BIG_PAGE", NULL);
+      if (big_page && big_page[0] == '0' && big_page[1] == '\0') {
+         fprintf(stderr, "radv: RADV_ATTR_RING_BIG_PAGE=0: attribute ring BIG_PAGE off (was %d)\n",
+                 info->discardable_allows_big_page);
+         info->discardable_allows_big_page = false;
+      }
+   }
+
    /* Compute the scratch WAVESIZE granularity in bytes. */
    info->scratch_wavesize_granularity_shift = info->gfx_level >= GFX11 ? 8 : 10;
    info->scratch_wavesize_granularity = BITFIELD_BIT(info->scratch_wavesize_granularity_shift);
